MID_EV11_075_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_075_m01_001: Cai! They're announcing the matchups for the main\ncompetition in the games!
MID_EV11_075_m01_002: So today's the day. I was thinking that it was nearly\ntime to hear about the next fights.
MID_EV11_075_m01_003: Do you get that information in advance, Ultand?
MID_EV11_075_m01_004: Well, I'm a temple official, but I didn't know what\nthe actual content of the announcements would be.
MID_EV11_075_m01_005: I'm a registered fighter in the games, so in the\ninterest of fairness I don't get insider information.
MID_EV11_075_m01_006: I guess the matchups are the hottest topic all over\nthe city.
MID_EV11_075_m01_007: They've posted them in the plaza, so let's get over\nthere as soon as we can.
MID_EV11_075_m01_008: Oh, wow. I did not expect this much of a crowd.\nThis really is a big deal, huh?
MID_EV11_075_m01_009: Is that the lineup for the main matches posted\nover there?
MID_EV11_075_m01_010: There are a lot of big names on the roster, a lot of\npeople a lot more ferocious than us.
MID_EV11_075_m01_011: Hard to believe I won't get my wish granted unless\nwe defeat all of them.
MID_EV11_075_m01_012: Well, you won't have to fight all of them. Some will\nget knocked out of the tournament by other teams.
MID_EV11_075_m01_013: Basically, if you can win three matches, you'll have\nwon the tournament.
MID_EV11_075_m01_014: Hmm... Seems like there's an empty roster slot.
MID_EV11_075_m01_015: Oh, here you are! Just in time for an emergency\nAnna administrative announcement!
MID_EV11_075_m01_016: Ribeira Winds! Excited about the reveal of the\nmatchups for the main event?
MID_EV11_075_m01_017: Uh, sure, but...didn't we already see them? They're\nposted right in front of us.
MID_EV11_075_m01_018: Never mind all that. Don't you want the message\ndelivered Anna-style?
MID_EV11_075_m01_019: Anna, which clan goes in the blank space on\nthe roster?
MID_EV11_075_m01_020: As it happens, we'll kick things off with another\nspecial match starring the White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV11_075_m01_021: The last slot is for the winner of that\nexhibition match.
MID_EV11_075_m01_022: Is Cruaidín fighting again? The one who beat the\nWhite-Maned Demon last time.
MID_EV11_075_m01_023: No. It'll be a fighter famous in Dagsion, someone\nknown as the Reaper.
MID_EV11_075_m01_024: The legendary Reaper? I've heard the stories.
MID_EV11_075_m01_025: It's said that no one who's faced him in the arena has\ncome out alive.
MID_EV11_075_m01_026: A fabled fighter who ensures certain death... It's no\nwonder he earned that nickname.
MID_EV11_075_m01_027: But I think it's been at least 10 years since anyone\nsaw him in the arena. I can't believe he's still alive.
MID_EV11_075_m01_028: Let me get this straight. We might end up fighting\nthis guy?
MID_EV11_075_m01_029: There's still some time before the main matches get \nstarted. I suggest you all prepare yourselves.
MID_EV11_042_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_042_m01_001: What a great match! I guess this means the empty\nslot on the roster's filled up.
MID_EV11_042_m01_002: Yeah! Bertrand was incredible, but I expected that.
MID_EV11_042_m01_034: And not just Bertrand. The fighters with him are\nincredible too.
MID_EV11_042_m01_016: They're all seasoned veterans. They've got hundreds\nof arena battles behind them.
MID_EV11_042_m01_017: But from what I saw, it seemed like they weren't\ncoordinating very well.
MID_EV11_042_m01_003: Anyway, I did some research on our next opponents.\nWant to hear about them?
MID_EV11_042_m01_035: They're called Rose Tempest, or something like\nthat, right?
MID_EV11_042_m01_004: Rose Tempest is Leda's group. We recently teamed\nup with them.
MID_EV11_042_m01_036: Looking at the composition of the team, I can see\nthat they're a bit reliant on magic.
MID_EV11_042_m01_005: So it could be that they don't react well to direct\nphysical attacks.
MID_EV11_042_m01_006: But I still think that the biggest threat we'll face will\nbe Leda's spellsongs.
MID_EV11_042_m01_037: Agreed. I've heard a lot about different types of\nspellsongs out there.
MID_EV11_042_m01_038: But Leda's are unusual. And she seems stronger than\nthe others who use them.
MID_EV11_042_m01_039: I guess only the best make it this far.
MID_EV11_042_m01_040: Right. Leda doesn't succeed because of luck. Her\nteam is really good.
MID_EV11_042_m01_031: Only one thing we can do now, Cai.
MID_EV11_042_m01_032: Yep. Same as always. We need to get stronger to\ngive ourselves the best chance to win.
MID_EV11_042_m01_033: Well, let's get to it, then!
MID_EV11_110_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_110_m01_001: Uh... You're Buccar, right? Leda's teammate?
MID_EV11_110_m01_002: You wanted to talk to me about something?
MID_EV11_110_m01_003: Kid, I am not sure I have any right to ask this of you.
MID_EV11_110_m01_004: But I want you to defeat milady. That is, I want you\nto stop Lady Leda.
MID_EV11_110_m01_005: What? Aren't you supposed to be on her side?
MID_EV11_110_m01_006: I am on her side. No one is more concerned for her\nthan me.
MID_EV11_110_m01_007: And that is why I want you to defeat her!
MID_EV11_110_m01_008: I can't believe it. Bertrand was the one who killed\nLeda's father?
MID_EV11_110_m01_009: And Leda's been out for revenge ever since.
MID_EV11_110_m01_010: Indeed. But now milady has stepped into far more\ndangerous territory.
MID_EV11_110_m01_011: I guess her goal is to kill Bertrand, then.
MID_EV11_110_m01_012: Yes, but even if she achieves that goal, it will not\nsave her. That is my fear. 
MID_EV11_110_m01_013: General Bertrand was a soldier, a great one. He was\nduty bound to do what he did.
MID_EV11_110_m01_014: My lord—Viceroy Guillermo—seemed to understand\nthis about him.
MID_EV11_110_m01_015: Milady can see it too. But hating Bertrand is the only\nthing that's allowed her to keep hold of her sanity.
MID_EV11_110_m01_016: Still, even if she gets her revenge, there are even\ngreater enemies lined up behind Bertrand.
MID_EV11_110_m01_017: And so milady will not stop...not until she is like a\njewel shattered into pieces.
MID_EV11_110_m01_018: I think there is only one hope for her—that she finds\ndefeat here and now so she cannot take her revenge.
MID_EV11_110_m01_019: Buccar... I can't make any promises.
MID_EV11_110_m01_020: I have my reasons for fighting too. And I don't\nintend to lose, even if I'm fighting Leda.
MID_EV11_110_m01_021: So, same as always, I'll do whatever I can do.
MID_EV11_110_m01_022: But I'm glad this is what your request turned out\nto be.
MID_EV11_110_m01_023: I was thinking you were gonna ask me to lose the\nfight on purpose.
MID_EV11_110_m01_024: Believe it or not, I do still have a bit of warrior's\npride left in my heart. I could never ask that of you.
MID_EV11_110_m01_025: I honestly cannot fathom your thought process.\nYou, of all people, encouraging our adversary?
MID_EV11_110_m01_026: You were listening in?
MID_EV11_110_m01_027: If someone defeats Miss Leda in the Heroic Games,\nyou think it will put an end to her quest for revenge?
MID_EV11_110_m01_028: How do I put this... Your plan is unsophisticated,\nnot to mention optimistic in the extreme.
MID_EV11_110_m01_029: Never mind the fact that your lady would be deeply\nsaddened if she knew what you were about.
MID_EV11_110_m01_030: Is this what you think loyalty is? It is not. This is an\nact of betrayal.
MID_EV11_110_m01_031: I do not care in the least. It is better than seeing\nmilady destroyed.
MID_EV11_110_m01_032: Mrr.
MID_EV11_110_m01_033: It's not that I don't understand how you feel...
MID_EV11_110_m01_034: But I believe the opposite. If she does not achieve the\nthing she wants most...there will be no saving her.
MID_EV11_110_m01_035: Moreover, it is my own lady's wish that Miss Leda\nfollow the path she chose to its destination.
MID_EV11_044_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_044_m01_001: The main event at last! Three more victories, and\nwe'll get you your wish.
MID_EV11_044_m01_002: I'll be giving it my absolute best for Aurora's sake.\nI want her to be happy too.
MID_EV11_044_m01_003: Right.
MID_EV11_044_m01_004: What's wrong? Are you alright? Where did all your\nusual upbeat energy go?
MID_EV11_044_m01_033: <NCA>Tell her what's wrong.
MID_EV11_044_m01_005: Ultand, it's just... It's all starting to sink in.\nThe consequences of what I'm doing, I mean.
MID_EV11_044_m01_006: I've been so focused on my own wish. But getting my\nwish means I'm crushing someone else's.
MID_EV11_044_m01_007: Cai, you're saying this now?
MID_EV11_044_m01_008: It's such a simple thing, but I hadn't thought about\nit before.
MID_EV11_044_m01_009: Leda hates Bertrand for killing her father. She thinks\nrevenge will settle her anger.
MID_EV11_044_m01_010: If she doesn't get her way, she'll be tied to the past,\nand she might not be able to move on.
MID_EV11_044_m01_011: I'm not sure my own wish matters compared to\nall that.
MID_EV11_044_m01_012: Cai, I want you to listen to me, really listen to me.
MID_EV11_044_m01_013: Before my grandpa returned to Ribeira, he was a\nseasoned tactician in the Aragonian army.
MID_EV11_044_m01_014: A tactician's job is a matter of life and death for\nmany soldiers on the battlefield.
MID_EV11_044_m01_015: Even if he wasn't directly involved in the battle,\nGrandpa's decisions would cost many their lives.
MID_EV11_044_m01_016: Not just enemies, but allies too. And sometimes\nbystanders, maybe.
MID_EV11_044_m01_017: Grandpa's choices lost many people their loved ones,\nso I think grudges might be a natural part of all that.
MID_EV11_044_m01_018: But you know what? If someone came looking for\nGrandpa to settle a score, I'd stand right by his side.
MID_EV11_044_m01_019: Because I love my grandpa, and he's the only family I\nhave left.
MID_EV11_044_m01_020: So however sad or angry Leda might be about her\nfather, I can't agree with what she's doing.
MID_EV11_044_m01_021: Tialla... It's amazing how much thought you've put\ninto all this.
MID_EV11_044_m01_022: Leda's wish is to kill someone because she thinks it\nwill quell her rage.
MID_EV11_044_m01_023: But, Cai, you're trying to save your father's life.
MID_EV11_044_m01_024: And if you do save him, you'll bring happiness to a\nlot of people—you and Aurora, and of course me too.
MID_EV11_044_m01_025: I prefer your wish, Cai. It's a beautiful, decent thing.
MID_EV11_044_m01_026: I don't think you're wrong for putting your wish first.\nSo let's make sure it comes true.
MID_EV11_044_m01_027: She's right. My thoughts exactly.
MID_EV11_044_m01_028: Besides, if you save Castor, I bet it'll make my mom\nreally happy too.
MID_EV11_044_m01_029: Ah...
MID_EV11_044_m01_030: Thank you both. You opened my eyes a little there.
MID_EV11_044_m01_031: Alright. Enough worrying. Let's get this done.
MID_EV11_044_m01_032: That's the spirit! If this were a determination contest,\nwe'd have already won! Right?
MID_EV11_083_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_083_m01_001: Huh. You showed up. I was hoping you'd drop out.
MID_EV11_083_m01_002: I understand how you feel, Leda. You have a goal\nyou won't let go of.
MID_EV11_083_m01_003: But I'm not giving up on my wish without a\nfight either.
MID_EV11_083_m01_004: So I'm here to settle this, the right way.
MID_EV11_083_m01_005: Then I guess there's nothing left to do but fight.\nToo bad. I was really starting to like you.
MID_EV11_083_m01_006: It's funny, I'm here so I can kill the man who killed\nmy father...and you're here to save your father's life.
MID_EV11_083_m01_007: Hehe. We're like characters from the plot of\na tragedy written for the stage.
MID_EV11_083_m01_008: But in the end, the moral of this story is simple—\nonly the strongest will see their selfish goal fulfilled.
MID_EV11_083_m01_009: Everyone fighting with me knows the score here.\nAnd we've made up our minds.
MID_EV11_083_m01_010: If we have to crush your hopes to win, so be it.
MID_EV11_083_m01_011: You have some nerve. But I'm sorry. Failure is not an\noption for me either.
MID_EV11_083_m01_012: I desire revenge, and that desire is the only thing\nthat has kept me alive until now.
MID_EV11_083_m01_013: The black hatred boiling in the deepest reaches of\nmy chest—that is the fuel that has sustained me.
MID_EV11_083_m01_014: You think I'd let you deny me my feelings, my\nthoughts...the very life I've come to live?
MID_EV11_083_m01_015: Loved by your parents, raised without hardship...\nWhen I see happy kids like you—
MID_EV11_083_m01_016: To be honest, it makes me hate you. You disgust me. 
MID_EV11_083_m01_017: Hahaha! Please forgive me. I think I'm going to be a\nlittle bit cruel today.
MID_EV11_083_m01_018: In fact, I might hurt you so much it makes you cry.\nBut that's only because I don't have any choice!
MID_EV11_045_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_045_m01_001: Oh, it's you... Well, I lost. You really are very strong.
MID_EV11_045_m01_002: But it doesn't change what I plan to do. I'm still going\nto kill that man.
MID_EV11_045_m01_003: I'm going to check out a few places here and there\nand look for my next opportunity.
MID_EV11_045_m01_004: You know, I spoke about this with Kalla once...
MID_EV11_045_m01_005: To hate someone passionately...it's not unlike being\nin love.
MID_EV11_045_m01_006: I don't really know that much about being in love.
MID_EV11_045_m01_007: Oh? Well, I'm sure you'll find out soon enough.
MID_EV11_045_m01_008: Whether you're asleep or awake, a single person\noccupies your every thought.
MID_EV11_045_m01_009: You hate them, but it doesn't end there. This person\ncontrols your actions, your heart...your everything.
MID_EV11_045_m01_010: This feeling drives you—drives everything about\nyou—and soon nothing else has meaning.
MID_EV11_045_m01_011: Eventually, you feel like you have to go along with it,\nbecause if you don't, you'll lose yourself entirely.
MID_EV11_045_m01_012: But, Leda, there are people who love you and care\nabout you.
MID_EV11_045_m01_013: I think Buccar was really worried when he saw what\nyou'd become.
MID_EV11_045_m01_014: Hm...
MID_EV11_045_m01_015: I think this is goodbye, Cai. I hope you get your wish.
MID_EV11_045_m01_016: I know I asked a great deal of you, Cai.
MID_EV11_045_m01_017: Hm? You're not with Leda?
MID_EV11_045_m01_018: I'm afraid Leda has dismissed me.
MID_EV11_045_m01_019: She did? But no one cares about her more than\nyou do.
MID_EV11_045_m01_020: Be that as it may, all she sees is an unforgivable act \nof betrayal.
MID_EV11_045_m01_021: Keeping her safe was my reason for living, so I truly\ndo not know what to do.
MID_EV11_045_m01_022: I would not give up on life, but I wonder... Where do\nI go from here?
MID_EV11_045_m01_023: This is just my way of looking at it, but I think Leda\nstill needs you, Buccar.
MID_EV11_045_m01_024: And, yeah, maybe she cut you loose, but she's not\nalways completely up-front about things.
MID_EV11_045_m01_025: Maybe she wants you to come after her.\nI don't know.
MID_EV11_045_m01_026: You could just go along with them. Tell them you\nhappen to be going the same way.
MID_EV11_045_m01_027: Ha! You think that'll work? Hehehehe. You might be\nright. I might have to give it a try.
MID_EV11_045_m01_028: Thanks, kid. You've been a great help. I will pay\nyou back for this someday.
MID_EV11_046_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_046_m01_001: Cai, got a sec? I think we need to talk.
MID_EV11_046_m01_002: What's going on, Gabriel? You sound so serious.
MID_EV11_046_m01_003: It's about your old man. It seems like... I don't know\nhow to say this. He hasn't got much time left.
MID_EV11_046_m01_004: What?! What are you saying?!
MID_EV11_046_m01_005: Every night, around midnight, he has these terrible\ncoughing fits. It's rough.
MID_EV11_046_m01_006: I've been keeping an eye on how he's doing awhile,\nand to be honest, he's not getting better.
MID_EV11_046_m01_007: Your dad tries to hide it, but I think he's coughing\nup blood, and a lot of it.
MID_EV11_046_m01_008: I've seen others get sick like this, but...no one who\ncould be helped.
MID_EV11_046_m01_009: And the thing is, when I ask him about it, the guy\nplays dumb. I don't think he wants me to know.
MID_EV11_046_m01_010: Going out on a limb, I'd say he's been dealing with\nthis awhile. You notice anything back home?
MID_EV11_046_m01_011: He...always used to go off somewhere during the\nnight. He wouldn't come back until daybreak.
MID_EV11_046_m01_012: Yeah... I guess he, uh, would've done anything to\nkeep you from finding out.
MID_EV11_046_m01_013: But why? Does my mom know about this?
MID_EV11_046_m01_014: I bet your parents didn't want you to worry.\nY'know, these things, they're always complicated.
MID_EV11_046_m01_015: But hey. Bear up, OK?
MID_EV11_046_m01_016: Looking after prisoners is my job. I'll bring in the best\ndoctor I can find.
MID_EV11_046_m01_017: I swear I'm going to do what I can. No need to start\ndespairing right now.
MID_EV11_046_m01_018: I'm just...letting you know, so if the worst happens,\nyou won't be totally caught off-guard.
MID_EV11_046_m01_019: Anyway, sorry for keeping you. I'd better get back to\nmy post.
MID_EV11_046_m01_020: Even if I win, my dad might not have long to live.
MID_EV11_046_m01_021: So why am I even doing this?